{
  "id": 414203474,
  "iid": 21301,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "pcapng: fixed UAF when handling pcap block read error",
  "description": "The issue can happen when the function `pcapng_read_darwin_legacy_block` successfully adds a Darwin PIB block to the `wth->dpibs`, but its caller (`pcapng_read_block`) encounters an unrelated error.\n\nIn this case, the Darwin PIB block will be unreferenced twice:\n\n1. By `pcap_open`, upon the failure of `pcapng_read_block`\n2. By `wtap_block_array_free(wth->dpibs)`, when the wth is closed.\n\nThis fix addresses the issue by incrementing the block's refcount once it has been added to the `wtap->dpibs` array.\n\nTested with Address Sanitizer `-DENABLE_ASAN=on`) on the following files:\n\n1. [19734-uaf.pcapng](/uploads/14d05d46f74bd7cd1fefe9899f52dbb8/19734-uaf.pcapng) - invalid file that causes UAF on Master (thanks to @dariusd0 )\n2. [tcpdump_k_pktap_written_exp_21_40.pcapng](/uploads/cda6b9ab214c200cb31aa30fe977d39d/tcpdump_k_pktap_written_exp_21_40.pcapng) - valid file to ensure that the functionality is preserved.",
  "state": "merged",
